module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.import_collides_with_a_kernel_name

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data import_collides_with_a_kernel_name: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "import_collides_with_a_kernel_name" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**import collides with a kernel name** (INVALID STATE: a module authors `import M \{ Optional \}` where M declares a type named Optional that is not the kernel mint, while the kernel Optional (`std.optional`, minted by `v1.compiler.infer` `kernel_optional_type_node`) is also in the closure. The type environment's by-name overlay (`overlay_skips_kernel_name`: kernel wins) and the interned-identity lookup (`lookup_binding`: import can win) then type the same spelling two ways. The emitted module rendered `HeldChoice<present_value>`, a leaked kernel type variable. Silent wrongness on the source path; rustc was the only wall.",

    "MEASURED by bright-swift-722 on gunbc#13454 (lane 2K-b). The collision declaration and its importer live under fixtures/ (`native_emission_controls_optional_collision`, `native_emission_controls_optional_importer`) and are compiled only as a fixture. A second Optional type must not sit in a source-root: leaf-keyed Optional typing then follows the last declarer in every floor closure.",

    "CHAIN RE-DERIVATION (§6b). The symptom is at emit (HeldChoice). The two lookups already disagree at resolve/infer. Unifying them under one precedence would pick one referent consistently and leave the other Optional type in the closure unused or mis-typed -- a second lie, not one rule. The earliest unjustified boundary is the authored import of a non-mint type that shares the mint's spelling. Refusal at that import is the construction.",

    "SCOPE OF THE WALL, from the census before the cut. Kernel-named IMPORTS are the ordinary corpus: String 3757, List 3294, Bool 3169, Int 1989, Present 997, Absent 965, Optional 372 (359 of them from `std.optional`). Refusing every kernel-named import would refuse the floor. TYPE DECLARATIONS of those names are few: Optional in the accepted corpus is `std.optional`; the colliding declaration is a fixture only; String is `v2.std.node` and `v2.std.text`; Int is `std.integer` and `v2.std.integer`. The wall fires only when the imported module DECLARES a type of that name AND a `kernel_mint_declaration_rows` row names a different DeclarationRef as the mint (module_path AND decl_name). A row for owner.Maybe does not exempt importing owner.Optional. Ambiguous mint rows refuse as KernelMintDeclarationAmbiguousAtImport, not as a guessed module. Dual-representation imports (`v2.std.text` String) stay with `carrier_by_spelling`.",

    "CURRENT RUNG: mechanically preventable. Discriminating RED: `test.claim.infer_kernel_import_collision_witness` `importing_a_non_mint_optional_refuses_at_the_import` (ImportCollidesWithKernelName at the import). Positive controls: a non-kernel name imported from the same collision module is accepted; importing the mint (`std.optional` Optional) compiles clean. The Maybe-row exemption hole is refused by `a_mint_row_for_owner_maybe_does_not_exempt_importing_owner_optional`. CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- an Accepted program cannot contain the colliding import. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the same refusal is derived on the v2 resolve path for every kernel-mint spelling, so the two compilers cannot disagree on whether the import is writable.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.literal_elaboration", decl_name: "kernel_named_import_standing", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.resolve", decl_name: "imported_type_collides_with_kernel_mint", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v1.compiler.resolve", decl_name: "resolve_import", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.infer_kernel_import_collision_witness", decl_name: "importing_a_non_mint_optional_refuses_at_the_import", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.structural_realization_bindings", decl_name: "kernel_mint_declaration_rows", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
